module uim.myname.domain.types;

/// Types for the domain layer of the application.
/// Domain types define the fundamental data structures and primitive types used throughout the domain layer.
/// They provide a consistent and standardized way to represent and manipulate domain-specific data.
/// By using well-defined domain types, developers can ensure type safety, improve code readability, and reduce the likelihood of errors.
/// Domain types serve as the building blocks for entities, value objects, and domain services, enabling a more robust and maintainable domain model.
/// They help to enforce business rules and constraints at the type level, promoting a more expressive and self-documenting codebase.
/// In essence, domain types provide a foundation for creating a flexible, maintainable, and high-quality domain layer that can effectively support the evolving needs of the business.
